From eb2da65d64d509ef396f79112e03116e61bde220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:08:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] prose_portal: the desktop's PATH and HOME for the commands it
 runs

A system job gets no environment from launch_daemon, which only sets
SAFEMODE; the desktop's PATH comes from SetupEnvironment, sourced by the
user session's jobs, and the portal is not one of them. A command run
through the portal therefore had no PATH at all (env showed none), so
`StyledEdit` was "command not found" while /boot/system/apps/StyledEdit
ran; it happened to resolve on the very first boot, where the package
was activated late. Sourcing SetupEnvironment from the launch job was
tried first and is worse: the script asks `locale` and `finddir`, which
want servers that are not up when a system job starts, Job::Launch()
waited on it, and one boot in three had no portal daemon at all. The
daemon now sets PATH and HOME itself where nothing did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0071-prose-portal-the-desktop-s-path-and-home-for-the-commands-it.patch e09677325edeeefacc75ac10db37d0501bb35701d21e5d7753fdca9bb92b1201
---
 src/servers/prose_portal/prose_portal.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/servers/prose_portal/prose_portal.cpp b/src/servers/prose_portal/prose_portal.cpp
index 9a38a47812..8ff85ee47f 100644
--- a/src/servers/prose_portal/prose_portal.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/prose_portal/prose_portal.cpp
@@ -290,6 +290,18 @@ main()
 {
 	openlog("prose_portal", 0, LOG_DAEMON);
 
+	// launch_daemon gives a system job no environment: the desktop's PATH
+	// comes from SetupEnvironment, which the user session's jobs source and
+	// this one is not among them. Sourcing it from the launch file is no
+	// good either: the script asks locale and finddir, which want servers
+	// that are not up when this starts, and the job then never launched.
+	// So a command run here had no PATH and could not find
+	// /boot/system/apps. The desktop's values, where nothing set them.
+	setenv("HOME", "/boot/home", 0);
+	setenv("PATH", "/boot/home/config/non-packaged/bin:/boot/home/config/bin:"
+		"/boot/home/config/apps:/boot/system/non-packaged/bin:/boot/system/bin:"
+		"/bin:/boot/system/apps:/boot/system/preferences", 0);
+
 	struct stat stopFile;
 	if (stat(kStopFile, &stopFile) == 0) {
 		syslog(LOG_INFO, "prose_portal: %s is there; not answering\n", kStopFile);
